# UI8Kit primitives — {{runtimeTitle}}

Primitives live in `{kit}` (one folder per primitive, generated code: do not edit by hand).
Import them from there: {{importHint}}

## 1. Use a primitive instead of raw HTML

Where a primitive exists for an element, use the primitive, never the raw tag:

| Primitive | Renders |
| --- | --- |
{{primitiveTable}}

Raw HTML is fine only for elements no primitive covers.

## 2. `tag` accepts only real HTML5 tags

`Box` and `Text` choose their element with `tag`. Pass only a real HTML5 tag from the allowed list
(never a component name, custom element or made-up tag):

{{tagGroups}}

## 3. Static ARIA via props

Set ARIA through the primitive's typed props (e.g. {{ariaExamples}}), as static values.
Do not hand-write `role`/`aria-*` that a primitive already renders (`Icon` sets `aria-hidden`
or `role="img"` + `aria-label` from `label`; `Switch` sets `role="switch"`).

## 4. Colors only via shadcn token classes

Style with token utility classes only: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-primary`,
`text-primary-foreground`, `bg-secondary`, `bg-muted`, `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-accent`,
`bg-destructive`, `border-border`, `border-input`, `ring-ring`, `bg-card`, `bg-popover`, …
No palette colors (`bg-blue-500`), no hex/rgb/hsl values, no arbitrary color classes (`bg-[#fff]`),
no inline `style` colors.

## 5. Spacing: 8 + 4 rule

- Spacing (padding, margin, gap, space-*) uses the 8px step: Tailwind `2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 16, …`
  (`p-2` = 8px, `gap-4` = 16px).
- The 4px step (`1`, e.g. `px-1`, `gap-1`) is allowed only inside controls (button, input,
  select, checkbox, badge-like inline control content).
- No half-steps (`p-0.5`, `p-1.5`, `p-2.5`, …), no odd steps (`p-3`, `p-5`, `p-7`), no arbitrary
  px values (`p-[13px]`, `mt-[7px]`).

## 6. Icons: Lucide inside `Icon`

Use Lucide icons ({{lucidePackage}}) as the child of the `Icon` primitive; size via `Icon` `size`
(`xs`, `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`). Give `label` when the icon carries meaning; omit it for
decorative icons.

{{example}}

